Z||000000||dodger||12-26-1999||01:24 PM||||I'm a new owner of an '86 SE 2.8. I love it.<BR>80,000 original miles and SUPER clean. It runs great except for one thing...it hesitates when taking off from a stop, or when shifting to a higher gear. I have to  tach-up a little bit and slip the clutch. Other symptoms are high idle (1250rpm) and it won't run soothly when in first gear going very slow like in parking lots...it it jerks and I have to use the clutch. Thaks for your help...dodger. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-26-1999||08:03 PM||||do the usuall complete search for vacuum leaks. check static timing according to manual. Those are the first two things to do.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||12-27-1999||12:39 PM||||Sounds like a good candidate for EGR tube and a good de-carbonizing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||12-27-1999||01:09 PM||||I'd check the timing too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kornholio||12-27-1999||02:06 PM||||After I cleaned my throttle body, my car hasn't hessitated when I step on the gas from a stop position.||||reg||14
